# Domain

Supports `.project-overview.mdc` and `architecture.mdc`. This layer is the core business model.

## What belongs here

TypeScript business domain:

- Entities and aggregates (Conversation, Ticket, KnowledgeDocument)
- Value objects and branded IDs
- Domain services (assignment, SLA, escalation policy)
- Domain events (facts that already happened)
- Domain errors (`InvalidConversationStateError`)

Python AI domain covers AI concepts (retrieval/guardrail outcomes, tool-call intents) — not Conversation/Ticket aggregates, not Prisma models, and not provider SDK types.

Do not put prompts, agents, RAG pipelines, or LLM orchestration in TypeScript domain.

## Invariants

Encode rules in the domain, not in controllers:

- Conversation and ticket state transitions
- Escalation and agent assignment
- SLA
- Knowledge document lifecycle

Reject illegal transitions with domain errors. Do not “fix” them in the API layer.

## Purity

Domain must not depend on Express/Fastify, FastAPI, Prisma, SQLAlchemy, PostgreSQL, Redis, LLM SDKs, LangChain, LangGraph, LlamaIndex, embedding/vector SDKs, external APIs, or queue libraries.

No I/O, no HTTP, no tokens, no prompt strings, no SQL.

## Events

Domain events are past-tense facts: `ConversationEscalated`, `TicketResolved`. They do not perform side effects. Application/adapters publish and consume them.
